(4079915, 579343, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: The first thing that jumps out to me is the lack of true whites.  This either indicates underexposure, or a color cast.  I think increasing the contrast could have helped somewhat.  A bit more saturation could have made that beak pop a bit too.  Composition is a nice tight crop.<br/> <br/>The feel: Has a decent feel for a patriotic eagle shot.<br/> <br/>The game: I think the quote is a bit wordy.  That has nothing to do with photography though.  Did you resize after you placed the text?  If so, that''s the culprit for your soft letters.  Never resize text if it can be helped.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-09-11 00:16:29.</i></td>', 'The technicals: The first thing that jumps out to me is the lack of true whites.  This either indicates underexposure, or a color cast.  I think increasing the contrast could have helped somewhat.  A bit more saturation could have made that beak pop a bit too.  Composition is a nice tight crop. The feel: Has a decent feel for a patriotic eagle shot. The game: I think the quote is a bit wordy.  That has nothing to do with photography though.  Did you resize after you placed the text?  If so, that''s the culprit for your soft letters.  Never resize text if it can be helped.', '2007-09-11 01:15:43.000000', '2007-09-11 01:16:29.000000', 0),
