(4086018, 579315, 45475, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Delta_6:</b></div><hr/><i> Some cruel comments on this one ...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Gosh, I guess that''s in reference to mine. Apologies if my comment seemed cruel. It certainly wasn''t my intention to be. Just that Shakespeare is much easier heard than read, and I still don''t quite know what the heck he means!<br/> <br/>I do like your poster, although I think the sky suffers a little from exposure. Perhaps if the image were larger as well, we''d get to see more foreground detail? My eyes desperately search around those trees for the beauty I know is there, but can''t see.... <br/> <br/>Wait, maybe that was the idea...?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-09-12 21:53:22.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Delta_6: Some cruel comments on this one ...  Gosh, I guess that''s in reference to mine. Apologies if my comment seemed cruel. It certainly wasn''t my intention to be. Just that Shakespeare is much easier heard than read, and I still don''t quite know what the heck he means! I do like your poster, although I think the sky suffers a little from exposure. Perhaps if the image were larger as well, we''d get to see more foreground detail? My eyes desperately search around those trees for the beauty I know is there, but can''t see....  Wait, maybe that was the idea...?', '2007-09-12 22:49:31.000000', '2007-09-12 22:53:22.000000', 0),
